Hi Phil,

In my sample code I have 60 items, 30 at each moment with items 21:30 and 31:40 being the same between moments. I wrote the model like below but I keep getting a message about constraining fixed parameters. I know how to model such situation using multigroup but I would like to take the covariance between the latent variables of the two moments into account. Am I missing something?

I think you may want F2 to be defined as F2=21-60; otherwise, the a1 parameters will be fixed at the values of 0. That is, if I'm understanding your model correctly....

Responses to itens 1:30 are collected at time 1 and
Responses to itens 31:60 are collected at time 2 under the condition that itens 21:30==31:40 to fix the scale. F2 should only be influenced by itens of the time 2. Why a1's get fixed at zero?

Regards,

Hugo

